  "source_lineage": [
    "Pinned preprocess backward allocates duvqk and splits du/dv/dq/dk into its storage, then attention and SiLU write those subviews.",
    "The original triton_addmm_bwd receives x=normed_x,w=uvqk_weight,dz=duvqk.",
    "Pinned function enqueues dy=sum(dz,dim0), dw=mm(x.T,dz), then dx=mm(dz,w.T); return tuple is dx,dw,dy.",
    "Wrapper output map names the first return d_normed_x. There is no alpha, beta, bias or residual add in this DX formula.",
    "Caller passes that first return directly as dy to triton_weighted_layer_norm_bwd; adjacent saved scan32 repeats the large DX extrema."
  ],
  "observation_timing": [
    "For STU1 the capturing wrapper delegates to the generic deferred monitor because full pre/post backing snapshots target only STU2.",
    "Generic monitor binds the original inputs, enqueues before reductions, calls the original function once, enqueues after reductions, and returns outputs.",
    "Reductions run on each tensor device current autograd stream. With normal per-stream FIFO, before reductions precede the enqueued GEMMs and after reductions follow them.",
    "record_stream protects allocation lifetime; it is not an immutability lock, cross-stream dependency, or certificate of values consumed by native GEMM.",
    "Only small extrema tensors survive to the final stream-joined readback. STU1 original input/output storages are not independently snapshotted here.",
    "Later writes on the same ordered stream should follow the after reduction. Cross-stream wild stores, broken dependencies or backend stream-contract violations can still affect input/output observations."
  ],
  "non_aliasing_limits": "Source torch.mm allocates an output, and expected semantics do not alias its inputs. STU1 saved scalar summaries do not certify physical non-overlap, input immutability or complete backing-byte identity. No pre/post-copy independence claim from STU2 transfers to STU1.",
  "unresolved_alternatives": [
    "Input mutation between its before reduction and native consumption (including overlapping writers or incorrect stream dependencies).",
    "Wrong GEMM result or wrong/stale output content, including allocator/native implementation or lower-level fault.",
    "Output mutation after GEMM but before its after reduction, especially an unordered writer.",
    "Corrupted diagnostic reduction or endpoint storage. Adjacent output/input extrema and downstream magnification are supporting witnesses, not a raw-word oracle."
  ],
  "trigger_gap": "All values here are finite and below the frozen absolute threshold1e6; this conditional matrix-product violation is outside that trigger, explaining why NP1000 bounded completion did not save a raw payload.",
  "limits": [
    "These are conditional bounds on the recorded operand extrema, not an independently recomputed output or proof of operands consumed by the native kernel.",
    "STU1 records deferred scalar scans of original operands and outputs. It has no retained before/after full operand snapshots or byte-continuity checks; only STU2 has the extra projection capture.",
    "Per-stream ordering and retained references do not rule out cross-stream mutation, internal operand-delivery faults, output faults, or scalar-scan faults.",
    "Exact-real-arithmetic triangle bounds are reported separately from a declared1percent allowance. No precise native accumulation algorithm or hardware error model is assumed.",
    "The large step583 DX value precedes the later LayerNorm and selected additional Linear gradient spike; later LayerNorm sensitivity alone does not explain this earlier inconsistency.",
    "No firmware, driver, compiler, BLAS or hardware culprit is assigned; this remains current corrected-driver/MES0x7b evidence."
  ],
